      "stageRecord": "Construct the matrix IP with the pronoun I in Spec-IP and the completed VP as the complement of a silent present-tense I. As in the embedded clause, the subject is base-generated in Spec-IP; predication by the VP headed by wonder assigns this subject the external Experiencer theta-role. Matrix I licenses the first-person singular present form wonder without moving the verb out of V, and it governs the subject position and assigns nominative Case to the pronoun. Finally, project a silent declarative C above the matrix IP. This C types the whole sentence as declarative, while whether continues to type only the selected embedded clause as interrogative. Consequently, the sentence contains neither matrix subject–auxiliary inversion nor a matrix question dependency. Each subject bears one theta-role and nominative Case, and the embedded CP bears the selected internal theta-role. The completed tree pronounces I wonder whether John left in that order.",
